    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0835" n="823" xml:id="pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.4181/14: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Casablanca</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Goold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Casablanca</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-04T12:00:00+01:00">September 4,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 4—11:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. My telegram 102, August 28. The Resident General has answered the Belgian
                    Consul General saying that the matter does not concern the Dean of the Consular
                    Corps of Casablanca but the French, Moroccan, and the British Governments
                    exclusively.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Goold</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
